From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:37:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tccgen: init_putz without CONFIG_TCC_BCHECK

The inline zero-filling of local initializers tested do_bounds_check,
a field that only exists with CONFIG_TCC_BCHECK; a tcc configured with
--config-bcheck=no (the guest tcc of tinycc-os-kernel) did not build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tccgen.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tccgen.c b/tccgen.c
index d243573..53553cb 100644
--- a/tccgen.c
+++ b/tccgen.c
@@ -8457,7 +8457,13 @@ static void init_putz(init_params *p, unsigned long c, int size)
     if (p->sec) {
         /* nothing to do because globals are already set to zero */
 #ifdef TCC_TARGET_NATIVE_STRUCT_COPY
-    } else if (!tcc_state->do_bounds_check) {
+    } else if (
+#ifdef CONFIG_TCC_BCHECK
+               !tcc_state->do_bounds_check
+#else
+               1
+#endif
+               ) {
         /* inline, like GCC: no call into a libc the code may not have */
         vseti(VT_LOCAL, c);
         vpushi(0);
